  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funding to front line health actors in response to the Gaza Crisis.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The British Red Cross (BRC) is an established partner with and through whom the FCDO provides funding to Red Cross-National Societies in several high-risk countries. BRC will provide direct support to the Palestinian Red Crescent Society (PRCS) and the Egyptian Red Crescent Society (ERCS) as needed. PRCS is the principal front line health actor in Gaza and the West Bank, including running hospitals and primary health clinics, and providing the official ambulance service across the OPTs. The Egyptian Red Crescent Society (ERCS) has a longstanding partnership and close working relationship with the British Red Cross. ERCS manages all humanitarian assistance arriving in to and dispatched from, Al Arish, in northern Egypt. Their role is indispensable in ensuring aid enters Gaza from Egypt.</narrative>
  </description>
